# Can a held-orientation plan be attempted from this start, to this goal?
#
# A hold keeps the orientation AT THE GOAL'S VALUE, so a goal that disagrees
# with the start on the held components is asking for two orientations at once.
# This answers that without planning and without moving anything.
#
# plan_to_pose runs the SAME check itself and refuses with
# CONSTRAINT_UNSATISFIABLE, so calling this first is optional — it exists so a
# caller can find out before committing to a goal, and get the measured number
# rather than a status code.
geometry_msgs/Pose target
float64[] start_joints        # REQUIRED, same contract as the plan actions
OrientationHold hold
---
bool satisfied                # true: the constrained plan can be attempted
string message                # empty when clean; explains the refusal when not
float64 deviation_deg         # measured disagreement between start and goal
float64 limit_deg             # the configured tolerance it is measured against
bool marginal                 # satisfied, but close enough to the limit to warn

# deviation_deg counts only what the hold actually holds: under HOLD_LEVEL it is
# the TILT, hypot(rx, ry) — the part of the rotation not about base Z — so a
# pure yaw difference reads 0 and is correctly allowed. Under HOLD_FIXED it is
# the full angle. There is no per-axis breakdown any more because there are no
# per-axis holds; the old worst_axis/worst_error fields described an interface
# that no longer exists.
